.\" Manpage for BOB audit profile files
.TH BOB-PROFILE 5 "2026-10-29" "BOB 0.28.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
bob-profile \- BOB audit profile file format (severity overrides per finding key)
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I ~/.config/bob/profiles/\fINAME\fI.conf
.PP
Built-in profiles (shipped with the package):
.RS
.IR bob/data/profiles/server.conf
.PP
.IR bob/data/profiles/desktop.conf
.PP
.IR bob/data/profiles/container.conf
.PP
.IR bob/data/profiles/workstation.conf
" (first-class profile since v0.8.1 \(em business workstation semantics)"
.RE
.PP
Selection: invoke
.B bob --profile=NAME
or set the default via the configuration file. User profiles override
built-in profiles with the same name.
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
An audit profile lets the operator adjust the severity of specific findings
to match the deployment context. A
.B desktop
machine has different tradeoffs than a public-facing
.BR server ;
.B container
images don't run an SSH server at all.
.PP
Each profile file is an INI-like text format with one or more sections.
The
.B [profile]
section declares metadata; the
.B [overrides]
section maps finding keys to new severity levels; the
.B [skip_sections]
section lists whole sections not to run.
.PP
A profile may
.B extend
another profile to inherit its overrides.
.
.SH FILE FORMAT
.SS [profile]
.TP
.B name
Profile identifier (e.g.
.IR workstation ).
Defaults to the file's basename without extension.
.TP
.B description
Free-text description (no CLI surface; visible in the file and in audit
profile-loading log messages).
.TP
.B extends
.RB ( optional )
Name of a parent profile to inherit from (its overrides and skipped sections).
Up to 8 levels of inheritance are allowed (see
.B _MAX_EXTENDS_DEPTH
in
.BR bob/profiles.py ).
A cycle or a deeper chain makes the profile fail to load:
.B bob
warns and runs that audit with
.BR server .
.SS [overrides]
One line per override:
.PP
.RS
.B \fIfinding.key\fR = \fIlevel\fR
.RE
.PP
where
.I level
is one of:
.TP
.B info
Demote the finding to INFO. It no longer counts as a warning or an alert and
does not deduct from the score.
.TP
.B warn
Force WARN level (default for most checks).
.TP
.B alert
Force ALERT level (counts as "action required" in the summary box and exit
code 2).
.TP
.B skip
Skip the finding entirely. The check still runs but no finding is emitted
for this key.
.PP
Keys not listed in
.B [overrides]
keep their default severity. A key must match exactly: an override written
under a former name of a key has no effect (unlike
.IR ignore.yml ,
which still honours the former names it knows).
.SS [skip_sections]
One section name per line (the names
.B bob \-\-check=list
prints). A listed section does not run at all, so none of its findings or
deductions appear. The built-in
.B container
profile uses this section.
.
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.I ~/.config/bob/profiles/headless-server.conf
.PP
.RS
.EX
[profile]
name        = headless-server
description = Server with no GUI: ignore desktop-only findings
extends     = server

[overrides]
ssh.x11.forwarding.server      = skip
ssh.allow_tcp_forwarding       = info
kernel_hardening.dmesg_exposed = alert
.EE
.RE
.
.SH PROFILE FILE DISCOVERY
.B bob
searches in this order:
.PP
.RS 4
.IP 1. 4
.IR ~/.config/bob/profiles/ \fINAME\fI.conf
(user override, takes precedence)
.IP 2. 4
.IR bob/data/profiles/ \fINAME\fI.conf
(built-in, shipped with the package)
.RE
.PP
The first match wins.
.
.SH SHIPPED PROFILES (overview)
.TP
.B server
Default. No overrides: every finding at its full severity. Used when no profile
is given or saved, unless
.B display-manager.service
is active (then
.BR desktop ).
.TP
.B desktop
Extends
.B server
and downgrades 35 findings to INFO, among them SSH password authentication,
X11 and TCP forwarding, MaxAuthTries and LoginGraceTime, automatic updates, a
missing backup, auditd, AppArmor without an enforcing profile, Secure Boot,
the freshness of rootkit / ClamAV / file-integrity scans, and services exposed
on the local network.
.TP
.B container
Extends
.B desktop
and skips 17 host-level sections (hardening, kernel_modules, kernel_hardening,
secure_boot, raspberry_pi, auditd, suid_audit, docker_hardening, rootkit,
file_integrity, disk, memory, fail2ban, clamav, ntp, mac_policy, backup) \(em
meant for container images and CI environments where filesystem and kernel
state are not auditable.
.TP
.B workstation
First-class business-tier profile since v0.8.1 (no longer an alias to
.BR desktop ).
Loads
.B workstation.conf ,
which keeps backup / auditd / MAC-enforce findings at WARN while relaxing the
same SSH / clamav / rootkit / file-integrity ergonomics as
.BR desktop .
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bob (1),
.BR bob.conf (5).
.PP
Full list of available finding keys:
.B bob --explain list
.PP
Per-key documentation:
.B bob --explain KEY
